      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JdkClientHttpRequestFactory",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " connects "
        ],
        [
          "RestClient",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " to Java\u2019s "
        ],
        [
          "HttpClient",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Connection and read timeouts limit different parts of a call."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Provider request and response records describe the remote contract."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Database entities describe stored data."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-note-2-part-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Keeping them separate prevents a storage change from changing the provider payload."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-external-apis-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Read and create a provider post",
        "language": "java",
        "description": [
          "Each tab names a file relative to the project root. Java `17` and Maven are required. `mvn spring-boot:run` starts this example after its external requirements are configured.",
          "The project uses Java 17+, Spring Boot 3.5, and `spring-boot-starter-web`.",
          "`PostApiClient.java` belongs in `src/main/java/com/example/demo`, below the application\u2019s scanned package.",
          "JSONPlaceholder is a public demonstration provider.",
          "It simulates writes and does not save a created post permanently.",
          "An injected `PostApiClient` can call `read(1)` or `create(new PostApiClient.NewPost(1, \"A title\", \"A body\"))`.",
          "The example uses demonstration text only."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "Spring supplies the builder once when it creates the service.",
          "Building the client does not send a request.",
          "`read` fills the `{id}` path variable and reads the response into `Post`.",
          "`create` writes `NewPost` as JSON and reads the returned JSON into `Post`.",
          "The JSON field names match the record component names.",
          "The provider assigns the response `id`.",
          "Both methods reject an empty response before the caller reads its fields.",
          "The methods return provider records.",
          "They do not create an application endpoint."
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/PostApiClient.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport java.net.http.HttpClient;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport org.springframework.http.MediaType;\nimport org.springframework.http.client.JdkClientHttpRequestFactory;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\nimport org.springframework.web.client.RestClient;\n\n@Service\npublic class PostApiClient {\n    private final RestClient client;\n\n    public PostApiClient(RestClient.Builder builder) {\n        HttpClient http = HttpClient.newBuilder()\n                .connectTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3)).build();\n        var factory = new JdkClientHttpRequestFactory(http);\n        factory.setReadTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(5));\n        this.client = builder.baseUrl(\"https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com\")\n                .requestFactory(factory).build();\n    }\n\n    public Post read(long id) {\n        if (id < 1) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Positive id required\");\n        Post post = client.get().uri(\"/posts/{id}\", id)\n                .retrieve().body(Post.class);\n        if (post == null) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Empty post response\");\n        return post;\n    }\n\n    public Post create(NewPost input) {\n        Post post = client.post().uri(\"/posts\")\n                .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON).body(input)\n                .retrieve().body(Post.class);\n        if (post == null) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Empty post response\");\n        return post;\n    }\n\n    public record NewPost(long userId, String title, String body) {}\n    public record Post(long userId, long id, String title, String body) {}\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
